# WN22-00-000150: Windows Server 2022 permissions for program file directories must conform to minimum requirements.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-00-000150-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 permissions for program file directories must conform to minimum requirements.`
    description `Changing the system's file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications. The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option "Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users" is set to "Disabled" (WN22-SO-000240). Satisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,file-acl,ntfs`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:AC-3(4)`
    control_objective `WN22-00-000150`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Maintain the default permissions for the program file directories and configure the Security Option "Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users" to "Disabled" (WN22-SO-000240). Default permissions: \Program Files and \Program Files (x86) Type - "Allow" for all Inherited from - "None" for all Principal - Access - Applies to TrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders SYSTEM - Modify - This folder only SYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only Admini`

    component_id `comp-windows-file-acl`

    impl_AC_3_4 `Windows Server implements AC-3(4) by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Program Files does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `C:\Program Files`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE exists_check
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_1
        allow_identities string not_contains `Everyone`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_2
        allow_identities string not_contains `Anonymous`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_3
        allow_identities string not_contains `Guest`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF exists_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
